<section id="v-dol" class="view">
<h1>DOL starter</h1>
<p class="lede">Direct-on-line means the motor is connected straight to the supply when the contactor closes. Two circuits do the job: a power circuit that carries the motor current, and a low-current control circuit that decides when the contactor closes.</p>
<p class="hint">Tap any component in either diagram to see what it is and why it is there.</p>
<div class="pair">
<div class="rig"><h3>Control circuit</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 150" role="img" aria-label="DOL control circuit with stop, start, seal-in contact, overload contact and coil K1">
<line class="rail" x1="14" y1="20" x2="14" y2="140"/><line class="rail" x1="346" y1="20" x2="346" y2="140"/>
<text class="lbl" x="6" y="14">L1</text><text class="lbl" x="334" y="14">L2</text>
<g id="dCtlW"></g>
<circle class="dot" cx="50" cy="60" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="90" cy="60" r="3.5"/><line id="dStopSym" class="sym" x1="50" y1="60" x2="90" y2="60"/><text class="lbl" x="50" y="30">Stop (NC)</text>
<circle class="dot" cx="140" cy="60" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="180" cy="60" r="3.5"/><line id="dStartSym" class="sym" x1="140" y1="60" x2="178" y2="46"/><text class="lbl" x="140" y="30">Start (NO)</text>
<circle class="dot" cx="140" cy="120" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="180" cy="120" r="3.5"/><line id="dKSym" class="sym" x1="140" y1="120" x2="178" y2="106"/><text class="lbl" x="126" y="142">K1 auxiliary (NO)</text>
<circle class="dot" cx="215" cy="60" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="245" cy="60" r="3.5"/><line id="dOlSym" class="sym" x1="215" y1="60" x2="245" y2="60"/><text class="lbl" x="205" y="30">Overload (NC)</text>
<circle id="dCoil" class="coil" cx="295" cy="60" r="18"/><text class="coiltxt" x="295" y="65" text-anchor="middle">K1</text><text class="lbl" x="262" y="94">Contactor coil</text>
</svg></div>
<div class="rig"><h3>Power circuit</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 262" role="img" aria-label="Three-phase power circuit with breaker, contactor contacts, overload relay and motor">
<g id="dPwrW"></g>
<text class="lbl" x="64" y="12">L1</text><text class="lbl" x="124" y="12">L2</text><text class="lbl" x="184" y="12">L3</text>
<rect class="box" x="40" y="42" width="180" height="20" rx="4"/><text class="boxt" x="130" y="57" text-anchor="middle">MCB (breaker)</text>
<circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="92" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="112" r="3.5"/><line id="dk0" class="sym" x1="70" y1="92" x2="83" y2="104"/>
<circle class="dot" cx="130" cy="92" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="130" cy="112" r="3.5"/><line id="dk1" class="sym" x1="130" y1="92" x2="143" y2="104"/>
<circle class="dot" cx="190" cy="92" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="190" cy="112" r="3.5"/><line id="dk2" class="sym" x1="190" y1="92" x2="203" y2="104"/>
<text class="lbl" x="232" y="106">K1 main contacts</text>
<rect id="dOlBox" class="box" x="40" y="136" width="180" height="20" rx="4"/><text class="boxt" x="130" y="151" text-anchor="middle">Overload relay</text>
<rect class="box" x="40" y="190" width="180" height="62" rx="10"/><text class="boxt" x="70" y="226" text-anchor="middle">M 3~</text>
<g id="dFan"><circle class="sym" cx="130" cy="221" r="20"/><line class="sym" x1="130" y1="221" x2="130" y2="203"/><line class="sym" x1="130" y1="221" x2="145" y2="230"/><line class="sym" x1="130" y1="221" x2="115" y2="230"/></g>
</svg></div>
</div>
<h2 class="sub">How it runs</h2>
<ol class="steps"><li>Press Start. Current flows through Stop and the overload contact to coil K1.</li><li>K1 pulls in. Its three main contacts close and the motor starts. Its auxiliary contact closes too.</li><li>Release Start. The auxiliary contact keeps K1 energized. This is the seal-in.</li><li>Press Stop, or trip the overload. The coil loses power, K1 drops out and the motor stops.</li></ol>
<div class="dock"><div id="info" class="info" hidden><button id="infoX" type="button" class="x" aria-label="Close explanation">Close</button><h3 id="infoT"></h3><p id="infoP"></p><p id="infoC"></p></div><p class="st" id="dStatus"></p><div class="btns"><button id="dStart" type="button">Start</button><button id="dStop" type="button">Stop</button><button id="dOl" type="button">Trip overload</button></div></div>
</section>
<section id="v-stardelta" class="view">
<h1>Star-delta starter</h1>
<p class="lede">Starting a large motor direct-on-line draws a very large current. A star-delta starter first connects the windings in star, so each winding gets about 58% of the line voltage and the line current is about one third. When a timer runs out it switches the windings to delta for full voltage. It only suits a motor whose windings are rated for delta at your supply voltage.</p>
<div class="pair">
<div class="rig"><h3>Control circuit</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 310" role="img" aria-label="Star-delta control circuit with contactors K1, K3, K2 and timer T1">
<line class="rail" x1="14" y1="6" x2="14" y2="300"/><line class="rail" x1="346" y1="6" x2="346" y2="300"/>
<g id="sdCtl"></g><g id="sdSym"></g>
</svg></div>
<div class="rig"><h3>Power circuit and windings</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 300" role="img" aria-label="Power circuit with motor windings shown in star or delta">
<g id="sdPwr"></g>
<text class="lbl" x="54" y="11">L1</text><text class="lbl" x="104" y="11">L2</text><text class="lbl" x="154" y="11">L3</text>
<circle class="dot" cx="60" cy="44" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="60" cy="64" r="3.5"/><line id="sdp0" class="sym" x1="60" y1="44" x2="60" y2="64"/>
<circle class="dot" cx="110" cy="44" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="110" cy="64" r="3.5"/><line id="sdp1" class="sym" x1="110" y1="44" x2="110" y2="64"/>
<circle class="dot" cx="160" cy="44" r="3.5"/><circle class="dot" cx="160" cy="64" r="3.5"/><line id="sdp2" class="sym" x1="160" y1="44" x2="160" y2="64"/>
<text class="lbl" x="185" y="58">K1 main contacts</text>
<rect class="box" x="20" y="108" width="320" height="180" rx="10"/>
<line id="sdD0" class="w" x1="110" y1="138" x2="62" y2="232"/><line id="sdD1" class="w" x1="62" y1="232" x2="158" y2="232"/><line id="sdD2" class="w" x1="158" y1="232" x2="110" y2="138"/>
<line id="sdA0" class="w hide" x1="110" y1="201" x2="110" y2="138"/><line id="sdA1" class="w hide" x1="110" y1="201" x2="62" y2="232"/><line id="sdA2" class="w hide" x1="110" y1="201" x2="158" y2="232"/>
<text class="boxt" id="sdMode" x="110" y="264" text-anchor="middle">Windings idle</text>
<text class="boxt" id="sdTK1" x="200" y="135"></text><text class="boxt" id="sdTK3" x="200" y="157"></text><text class="boxt" id="sdTK2" x="200" y="179"></text>
<text class="boxt" id="sdV" x="200" y="205"></text><text class="boxt" id="sdI" x="200" y="225"></text>
<g id="sdFan"><circle class="sym" cx="270" cy="262" r="18"/><line class="sym" x1="270" y1="262" x2="270" y2="245"/><line class="sym" x1="270" y1="262" x2="285" y2="271"/><line class="sym" x1="270" y1="262" x2="255" y2="271"/></g>
</svg></div>
</div>
<h2 class="sub">How it runs</h2>
<ol class="steps"><li>Press Start. K1 closes and the timer begins. K3 also closes, which joins the winding ends together: star.</li><li>Watch the timer bar. The motor runs slower and gently while it accelerates in star.</li><li>When the timer finishes, its contact opens the K3 rung and closes the K2 rung. K3 drops out and K2 closes: delta.</li><li>Each of K3 and K2 has a normally closed contact in the other’s rung, so they can never be closed together. That would short the supply.</li></ol>
<div class="dock"><p class="st" id="sdStatus"></p><div class="meter" aria-hidden="true"><div id="sdFill"></div></div><div class="btns"><button id="sdStart" type="button">Start</button><button id="sdStop" type="button">Stop</button><button id="sdOl" type="button">Trip overload</button></div></div>
</section>
<section id="v-fwdrev" class="view">
<h1>Forward-reverse control</h1>
<p class="lede">To reverse a three-phase motor you swap any two of the three phases. Two contactors do it: F connects L1, L2, L3 straight through, and R swaps L1 and L3. If both closed together they would short the supply, so each coil rung contains a normally closed auxiliary contact of the other contactor. That is electrical interlocking.</p>
<div class="pair">
<div class="rig"><h3>Control circuit</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 220" role="img" aria-label="Forward and reverse control rungs with interlocking contacts">
<line class="rail" x1="14" y1="10" x2="14" y2="210"/><line class="rail" x1="346" y1="10" x2="346" y2="210"/>
<text class="lbl" x="6" y="8">L1</text><text class="lbl" x="334" y="8">L2</text>
<g id="frCtl"></g><g id="frSym"></g>
</svg></div>
<div class="rig"><h3>Power connections</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 290" role="img" aria-label="Supply phases L1 L2 L3 connected to motor terminals U V W, straight for forward and swapped for reverse">
<g id="frPwr"></g>
<circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="40" r="4"/><circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="90" r="4"/><circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="140" r="4"/>
<circle class="dot" cx="290" cy="40" r="4"/><circle class="dot" cx="290" cy="90" r="4"/><circle class="dot" cx="290" cy="140" r="4"/>
<text class="lbl" x="44" y="44">L1</text><text class="lbl" x="44" y="94">L2</text><text class="lbl" x="44" y="144">L3</text>
<text class="lbl" x="300" y="44">U</text><text class="lbl" x="300" y="94">V</text><text class="lbl" x="300" y="144">W</text>
<text class="boxt" id="frPhase" x="180" y="190" text-anchor="middle">Stopped</text>
<g id="frFan"><circle class="sym" cx="180" cy="240" r="22"/><line class="sym" x1="180" y1="240" x2="180" y2="220"/><line class="sym" x1="180" y1="240" x2="197" y2="250"/><line class="sym" x1="180" y1="240" x2="163" y2="250"/></g>
<text class="lbl" x="130" y="282">3-phase motor</text>
</svg></div>
</div>
<h2 class="sub">Try this</h2>
<ol class="steps"><li>Press Fwd. F pulls in and the motor turns one way.</li><li>While it runs, hold Rev. Nothing happens, because F’s auxiliary contact in the Rev rung is open.</li><li>Press Stop, then Rev. R pulls in, L1 and L3 are swapped, and the motor turns the other way.</li><li>Trip the overload to watch both contactors drop out.</li></ol>
<div class="dock"><p class="st" id="frStatus"></p><div class="btns four"><button id="frFwd" type="button">Fwd</button><button id="frRev" type="button">Rev</button><button id="frStop" type="button">Stop</button><button id="frOl" type="button">Trip overload</button></div></div>
</section>
<section id="v-plc" class="view">
<h1>PLC ladder logic</h1>
<p class="lede">A PLC replaces relay wiring with a program. Each rung is a row of contacts that must pass power to an output coil. The PLC repeats a scan cycle: read the inputs, solve the rungs from top to bottom, then update the outputs. Tap the inputs in the bar at the bottom to flip them, and edit any rung to see what changes.</p>
<div class="exrow"><button type="button" data-ex="1">Example: Start/Stop</button><button type="button" data-ex="2">Example: Interlock</button><button type="button" data-ex="3">Example: Timer</button><button type="button" data-ex="0">Clear</button></div>
<div id="rungs"></div>
<button type="button" id="pAddR" class="runbtn">+ Add rung</button>
<h2 class="sub">Know your symbols</h2>
<dl class="legend">
<dt>NO contact (examine if on)</dt><dd>Passes power when its address is ON. This is the ladder version of a Start button or a relay contact that closes.</dd>
<dt>NC contact (examine if off)</dt><dd>Passes power when its address is OFF. Use it for Stop. The program needs it as NC so that pressing Stop (input ON) cuts power.</dd>
<dt>Parallel branch</dt><dd>Two contacts side by side. Either one can pass power, which is OR logic. A branch with Start and the motor’s own output is the seal-in.</dd>
<dt>Output coil</dt><dd>Turns its address ON when power reaches it, and OFF when it does not.</dd>
<dt>Timer T0 (TON, 3 s)</dt><dd>Its contact turns ON after its rung has had power for 3 seconds without a break. It resets as soon as power is lost.</dd>
<dt>Scan order</dt><dd>Rungs are solved top to bottom, once per scan. A contact that reads an output defined lower down sees last scan’s value.</dd>
</dl>
<div class="dock"><p class="st" id="pStatus"></p><div class="chips" id="pIn"></div><div class="chips" id="pOut"></div><div class="btns"><button id="pRun" type="button">Stop PLC</button><button id="pStep" type="button" disabled>Step one scan</button></div></div>
</section>
